From 2d975a1e8ee71e50ae889841a464a66b06c79701 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xingyi Zhang <zhangxingyi0@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:20:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Note that abukhalaf_2025_disaster_prep resp is a proportion

Its 11 resp values run 0 to 1 in 0.1 steps and mean 0% to 100% likelihood,
not 1st through 11th response option: the source study measured rising-scale
answers and converted them to percentages ("answers were translated into
percentages, for example, Strongly Disagree (0.0%)... Strongly Agree (100%)",
PLOS 10.1371/journal.pone.0310665). Nothing in the itemtext table said so, and
an empty option_text for all 33 rows gives a reader no way to tell.

Surfaced by the audit of the four earliest-uploaded itemtext tables,
ben-domingue/irw#1645.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 itemtext_issues.qmd | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/itemtext_issues.qmd b/itemtext_issues.qmd
index 590181d..1baae76 100644
--- a/itemtext_issues.qmd
+++ b/itemtext_issues.qmd
@@ -599,4 +599,11 @@ Only items 1-48 of this table are the RIASEC interest inventory the table is nam
 :::
 :::
 
+::: {.g-col-4 .dataset-item}
+::: {.callout-warning collapse='true'}
+## abukhalaf_2025_disaster_prep
+`resp` is a **proportion, not an ordinal level**: the source study measured its rising-scale answers and then converted them to percentages, so the 11 values run 0 to 1 in 0.1 steps and mean 0% to 100% likelihood rather than 1st through 11th response option. `option_text` is empty for every row by design -- the source labels no individual point on the slider
+:::
+:::
+
 :::
